**Construction 4.4 (actual selected use).** Choose the earned last
raw terminal $\ell=\lambda(k)$ and compute
$q=\widehat w_\ell$. Actually execute Add$(k,q)$, Hold, Read$(k)$,
consuming the complete transactions. Every terminal has gauge sign
$1$, so the real returned rational is $2q$, and both actual source
and predictor update by $w\mapsto w+q e_\ell$ in corresponding
coordinates. This adds exactly one Add, Hold and scalar Read and their
full payload/selector/copy costs. It is lawful even when $q=0$.
As a numerical state map it doubles one terminal and fixes the
others, with rational inverse halving that terminal. This inverse
calculation does not execute a physical undo. Callable access and
the selector are the retained paid context, not products of arithmetic.

